# PICACO: Pluralistic In-Context Value Alignment of LLMs via Total Correlation Optimization

The paper was published at [ICML 2026](https://icml.cc/virtual/2026/poster/64797) and is also available on [arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.16679).

## Optimize a Customized Meta-Instruction
Before running `main.py`, you may prepare:
- your intended values, a seed instruction, and other configurations in `constant.py`;
- a target LLM that inherits from the `Base_LM` class in `lms.py`
- a prompt set under `data/ica_train`;
- a demonstration set under `utils/demos`;
- a value evaluator in `vd.py`;
- (optional) an observation set under `utils`.

## Test Your Customized Meta-Instruction
You may refer to `picaco_infer.py` for inference and `utils/gpt_eval_*.py` for evaluation.

